":7,"opponent":"TB","home":true,"pf":13.0,"pa":43.0,"off_snaps":54,"epa_per_play":-0.2677,"pass_rate":0.6667,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6667,"def_epa_per_play":0.2118},{"week":8,"opponent":"GB","home":false,"pf":19.0,"pa":27.0,"off_snaps":70,"epa_per_play":-0.1489,"pass_rate":0.6714,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6296,"def_epa_per_play":0.05257}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2024,"team":"CLE","distance":0.9266,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.9422,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"IND","distance":0.9544,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Shane Steichen"},{"season":2023,"team":"BUF","distance":1.012,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"CIN","distance":1.051,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Zac Taylor"}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"LA","distance":0.3549,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Raheem Morris"},{"season":2023,"team":"NE","distance":0.3751,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"KC","distance":0.5034,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Steve Spagnuolo"},{"season":2022,"team":"MIN","distance":0.5849,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"DEN","distance":0.5984,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Panthers are 3-4 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 193 to 178. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 12th in EPA per play while the defense sits 21st in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the highest RPO rate and the lowest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Panthers offense has been a little above average by EPA per play so far. They have thrown more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score has not called for it. Schematically, they stand out for the highest RPO rate and the fewest backs in the backfield in the league. Bryce Young has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Tetairoa McMillan, who has drawn 26% of the targets.","defense":"The Panthers defense has been a little below average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 16th and 28th. Princely Umanmielen has led the way with 3 sacks. In terms of scheme, they have the lowest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Panthers have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 73% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 100% of field goals, which is the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into linebackers, about 20% of the money on the books. Their running backs were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Bryce Young has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,921 yards. Tetairoa McMillan has been the clear top target with 26% of the looks and 569 receiving yards. Chuba Hubbard has handled most of the work in the backfield with 76% of the carries. On defense, Princely Umanmielen leads the team with 3 sacks and Devin Lloyd has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Dave Canales is calling the offense as head coach and Ejiro Evero is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Browns and the 2024 Jets. Their defense looks most like the 2022 Rams under Raheem Morris and the 2023 Patriots.","trends":"The offense went from 26th in EPA per play in 2025 to 12th so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 23rd in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 21st so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was neutral-script pass rate, which went from 51% to 63%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}